{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1948","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1948","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1948\",\"parent_revision\":\"6140bff05630d8214108f9ab1c8fefad60935f28\",\"root_revision\":\"dd67298875de64680b9299fc3be346059af75cc467cf9fc38d8c3ed9b89c4145\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add stable schema_version wrapper and --demo flag to implementation_manager snapshot commands** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/abtop.md \u2014 pattern: --once snapshot mode and --demo synthetic data for scripting/CI/screenshot tests\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\n| Input | Condition | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Add schema_version top-level field to JSON output + --demo flag to implementation_manager CLI snapshot commands |\\n| Scope boundaries | DERIVABLE | Snapshot commands = JSON-producing commands: status, ready-tasks, list-features. claim-task and validate produce action results \u2014 scope is ambiguous for those two |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | implementation_manager.py fully read; Typer CLI with list-features, status, ready-tasks; all JSON output currently lacks versioning |\\n| Existing version field | AVAILABLE | sam_schema.core.models.Plan.version field exists (default \\\"1.0\\\", line 279 of models.py) but not surfaced in CLI output |\\n| Test coverage | MISSING | No test file for implementation_manager.py found under testpaths (tests, tests_sam, tests_backlog) |\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen any implementation_manager snapshot command (status, ready-tasks, list-features) runs:\\n\\n- The JSON output contains \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"1.0\\\" as the first field.\\n- Consumers can check output[\\\"schema_version\\\"] to detect when the schema has changed.\\n\\nWhen --demo is passed to a snapshot command:\\n\\n- The command exits 0 and prints valid example JSON matching the command's normal output shape.\\n- The demo output does not require a valid project path or existing task files.\\n- The demo output is clearly labeled (e.g., \\\"_demo\\\": true) so callers can distinguish it from live data.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run implementation_manager.py status /any/path any-slug 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert 'schema_version' in d\\\"` exits 0.\\n2. `uv run implementation_manager.py ready-tasks /any/path any-slug 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert 'schema_version' in d\\\"` exits 0.\\n3. `uv run implementation_manager.py list-features /any/path 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert 'schema_version' in d\\\"` exits 0.\\n4. `uv run implementation_manager.py status --demo | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert d.get('_demo') is True and 'schema_version' in d\\\"` exits 0 with no real path argument needed.\\n5. `uv run implementation_manager.py ready-tasks --demo | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert d.get('_demo') is True\\\"` exits 0.\\n6. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` exits 0 (no linting regressions).\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should schema_version also be added to claim-task and validate output (for consistency), or only the three snapshot commands?\\n- Should --demo data be a static Python dict in the source, or loaded from a fixture file?\\n- What schema bump policy applies: calendar-versioned, semver, or integer increment?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Plan.version field (line 279) |\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:typer |\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:python3-testing |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- No test file exists for implementation_manager.py. The pyproject.toml declares testpaths = [\\\"tests\\\", \\\"tests_sam\\\", \\\"tests_backlog\\\"] but no test module for implementation_manager was found. Adding a test module is in scope for this item.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 2 files touched with additive-only changes (new module-level constant, new field per output dict, new --demo flag per snapshot command). No new dependencies. Optional test file creation adds bounded scope.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py | Add _SCHEMA_VERSION = \\\"1.0\\\" module constant; inject into all output dicts; add --demo flag to status, ready-tasks, list-features |\\n| plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md | Update command reference examples to show schema_version in example output |\\n| New test module | No existing test file for implementation_manager.py found under tests, tests_sam, or tests_backlog |\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n- schema_version value: Use the string \\\"1.0\\\" initially, matching Plan.version default in sam_schema/core/models.py line 279. Define as _SCHEMA_VERSION: str = \\\"1.0\\\" at module level.\\n- Injection point: Each snapshot command builds an output dict before console.print(json.dumps(output, indent=2)). Add \\\"schema_version\\\": _SCHEMA_VERSION as the first key in each dict. Python 3.7+ dicts preserve insertion order.\\n- --demo flag: Add `demo: Annotated[bool, typer.Option(\\\"--demo\\\", help=\\\"Return example output without requiring a real project.\\\")] = False` to each snapshot command. When True, return a hard-coded fixture dict (same shape as normal output) with \\\"_demo\\\": True and \\\"schema_version\\\": _SCHEMA_VERSION added, without reading any files.\\n- Backward compatibility: Adding a field to a JSON object is non-breaking for consumers that access named keys.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an orchestration agent or CI script consuming implementation_manager JSON output, I want a stable schema_version field at the top of every response so I can detect breaking schema changes and safely parse the output, and a --demo flag so I can validate my parsing logic without needing a real project or task files.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py status` already prints a JSON snapshot once and exits (lines 1045-1069). However, `ready-tasks` (line 1072) and `validate` (line 1126) emit JSON to stdout without a stable wrapper schema, no `as_of_timestamp`, no `schema_version`, and no `--format yaml|markdown` option. CI dashboards and external snapshot consumers must re-implement parsing per command. There's no fixture-mode way to populate a synthetic plan for snapshot validation tests.\\n\\nSymptom: snapshot consumers (CI status badges, external dashboards reading `~/.dh/projects/*/plan/`) parse three different output shapes from three subcommands. Test fixtures must build full plan files instead of using a flag.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`implementation_manager.py status --format=json|yaml|markdown` supports all three formats with a stable wrapper: `{schema_version: \\\"1\\\", as_of: \\\"2026-04-25T...\\\", project: \\\"...\\\", feature: \\\"...\\\", data: {...}}`. New `--demo` flag populates synthetic data without requiring a real plan file (useful for screenshot tests and skill examples). The same wrapper is applied to `ready-tasks` and `validate` commands.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py status . my-feature --format=yaml`. Output is valid YAML beginning with `schema_version: '1'`. Run `... status . any --demo --format=json`. Output is a synthetic snapshot with at least one in-progress task and one ready task. `jq -r .schema_version` against any of the three commands' JSON output returns `1`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d1b01a3f0ffdecd9cfb97f72280c1e84e974729f6c8fc5fa955d455eeb350e41\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnJ1HQ\"}"}